    "authoredFrom": "Read from the case's input bytes: grund.toml (version 1, `[reference] strict = false`, default kinds and scan) and two files in the FS home that each open `# FS-001-login: User login` over a one-line body, citing nothing. The ID has two homes, so `show` refuses it as ambiguous, naming both sites in path order (§FS-show.2.2.1, §FS-errors.5.2.1), and so does `refs` wherever the tree it scans holds both (§FS-refs.4) — under the path argument a.md it scans one home and lists no hits (§FS-scan.path.refs); `list` keeps both, each marked duplicate (§FS-list.2); `check` reports the duplicate once at the first site (§FS-declarations.checks.duplicate, §FS-check.2.1), and the ID once as missing from the absent index (§FS-check.3.18.2, §FS-check.3.18.7) and as never cited (§FS-check.4.1), there too, in path, line and message order (§FS-errors.4.1). Nothing is cited, so `fmt` has nothing to wrap.",
